s processed state separately from applied state. RSM applies commands/session semantics and callbacks report completion.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-formation\",\n        \"B-history\",\n        \"B-application\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-formation\",\n        \"M-term\",\n        \"M-read\",\n        \"M-engine\",\n        \"M-node\",\n        \"M-update\",\n        \"M-rsmapply\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Ticks initiate campaigns only for eligible nonremoved full members and only after committed work is applied. Candidate increments term and self-votes; vote grants check saved vote and log freshness; known eligible responses elect a majority. Becoming leader resets replication progress, reconstructs pending configuration status and appends a no-op. Higher terms step down with a recent-leader vote-suppression exception; stale terms are discarded. CheckQuorum steps down when voters are inactive; transfer suppresses proposals and waits for target catch-up before TimeoutNow. Reset abandons prior votes, pending read confirmations and transfer but preserves committed history. Snapshot recovery restores membership; self removal steps down.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-context\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-transitions\",\n        \"M-term\",\n        \"M-peer\",\n        \"M-tick\",\n        \"M-transfer\",\n        \"M-checkquorum\",\n        \"M-members\",\n        \"M-restore\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Authority reset prevents counting prior-term progress, while the surviving committed log constrains election freshness and future replication. Applied membership defines voting support; single pending configuration and election blocking on unapplied commit connect application timing to quorum overlap. ReadIndex separately requires a current-term commit before asking voters to confirm authority. A matching heartbeat quorum releases queued read statuses; emitted readiness then needs a matching caller context and locally applied index. Pending confirmations are volatile and reset on authority changes; request completion is separately timed and correlated.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-read-admit\",\n        \"B-read-confirm\",\n        \"B-read-consume\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-context\",\n        \"F-commit\",\n        \"F-readpending\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-members\",\n        \"M-term\",\n        \"M-transitions\",\n        \"M-read\",\n        \"M-readqueue\",\n        \"M-confirm\",\n        \"M-batches\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Remote ReadIndex response context differs from local release when one confirmation releases a prefix.\",\n      \"Snapshot storage/transport and asynchronous recovery variants need deeper reading.\",\n      \"Membership acceptance validation and in-flight support across configuration transitions remain open.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation and authority paths and their supporting persistence, membership, recovery and consumption boundaries are traced; detailed variants remain open, not claimed complete.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"6f495e2577f543668597d1796bafe573\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"6f495e2577f543668597d1796bafe573\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use res