{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The existing queue test expects each released read status to retain its own context. The consumer also looks up readiness by the full context. I’ll test the remote boundary with two distinct origins: drop the first request’s heartbeat messages, then let a later request obtain quorum. This exercises prefix release without fabricating replies or changing protocol state.\n"}}
